      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_292dd4a2",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: dey_call_me_wong; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme uses a person of East Asian descent laughing while displaying the text 'dey call me wong' and 'sum ting wong,' which is a play on the Cantonese phrase meaning 'something is wrong.' The intent is to mock or stereotype East Asian individuals by implying that their speech or behavior is inherently incorrect or foolish. This aligns with anti-Asian racism tropes, particularly the 'accent mockery' and 'emasculation of Asian men' categories, as it reduces the individual to a caricature based on perceived linguistic or cultural traits. The image's exaggerated expression and the text's tone are designed to provoke laughter at the expense of the person's identity, making it a hateful meme targeting a specific ethnic group.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_15ca67a3"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
